Subject: [202605] Skip only unsupported AS7326 PSU fan target comparisons

These self-controlled PSU fans do not expose a target through PDDF. Keep
actual speed/status, presence, airflow and PSU voltage checks; exclude only
the two per-fan target-speed comparisons, without inventing target values.
A stopped fan still reports failed status through the existing PDDF API.
This does not provide independent detection of a slowly spinning fan.
Precedent: https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-buildimage/pull/8198
Verified upstream: 5ef9e45ccf7f004fb07bf3f9be2f471cf00573bf.

--- a/device/accton/x86_64-accton_as7326_56x-r0/system_health_monitoring_config.json
+++ b/device/accton/x86_64-accton_as7326_56x-r0/system_health_monitoring_config.json
@@ -2,7 +2,9 @@
     "services_to_ignore": [],
     "devices_to_ignore": [
         "asic",
-        "psu.temperature"
+        "psu.temperature",
+        "PSU1_FAN1.speed",
+        "PSU2_FAN1.speed"
 
     ],
     "user_defined_checkers": [],
